{"cv-basics":[{"id":"cv-basics-1","prompt":"You have 800 labelled images for a new task. What is the best starting point?","explanation":"Pretrained features transfer well; with little data, freezing most layers avoids overfitting.","type":"single","options":["Train a ResNet-50 from scratch","Fine-tune a pretrained backbone, starting with a frozen backbone and a new head","Use k-means on raw pixels","Train only on the 10 best images"],"answer":1},{"id":"cv-basics-2","prompt":"Horizontal flipping is always a safe augmentation.","explanation":"It depends on the invariances of the task: a flipped \"6\" or flipped text is no longer the same thing.","type":"tf","answer":false},{"id":"cv-basics-3","prompt":"When unfreezing a pretrained backbone, a common choice is to give it a learning rate that is…","explanation":"Pretrained weights are already good; large updates would destroy them.","type":"single","options":["about 10× lower than the new head's","10× higher than the head's","zero","the same as training from scratch"],"answer":0},{"id":"cv-basics-4","prompt":"What does MixUp do?","explanation":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tilde x=\\lambda x_i+(1-\\lambda)x_j</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"></span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.35em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.2222em;\"><span class=\"mord\">~</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">j</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, and the same for the one-hot labels.","type":"single","options":["Shuffles pixels within an image","Blends two images and their labels with the same mixing weight","Rotates images randomly","Removes the background"],"answer":1}],"detection-segmentation":[{"id":"detection-segmentation-1","prompt":"What is the IoU of boxes [0, 0, 10, 10] and [5, 5, 15, 15]? (three decimals)","explanation":"Intersection 25, union 175, so IoU = 25/175 ≈ 0.143.","type":"num","answer":0.143,"tol":0.002},{"id":"detection-segmentation-2","prompt":"What does non-maximum suppression remove?","explanation":"Detectors predict many overlapping boxes per object; NMS keeps the best one.","type":"single","options":["Lower-confidence boxes that overlap a higher-confidence box by more than a threshold","All boxes below 50% confidence","Boxes at the image edge","The background class"],"answer":0},{"id":"detection-segmentation-3","prompt":"Why does the focal loss help one-stage detectors?","explanation":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-(1-p_t)^\\gamma\\log p_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0556em;\">γ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> shrinks the loss of confidently correct predictions.","type":"single","options":["It speeds up inference","It down-weights the many easy background examples so training focuses on hard ones","It removes the need for anchors","It replaces NMS"],"answer":1},{"id":"detection-segmentation-4","prompt":"What gives U-Net its sharp segmentation boundaries?","explanation":"Fine spatial detail lost by downsampling is recovered from the encoder.","type":"single","options":["Skip connections that pass high-resolution encoder features to the decoder","A larger softmax","Max pooling","Removing the encoder"],"answer":0}],"vit-clip":[{"id":"vit-clip-1","prompt":"A 224×224 image split into 16×16 patches gives how many patch tokens?","explanation":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>224</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>16</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>14</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>196</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(224/16)^2=14^2=196</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">224/16</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">196</span></span></span></span>, plus a [CLS] token in the original ViT.","type":"num","answer":196,"tol":0},{"id":"vit-clip-2","prompt":"How does CLIP classify an image zero-shot?","explanation":"Image and text share an embedding space trained contrastively.","type":"single","options":["It was trained on every class name","It embeds prompts like \"a photo of a {label}\" and picks the one most similar to the image embedding","It runs a detector first","It asks a human"],"answer":1},{"id":"vit-clip-3","prompt":"In CLIP's training batch, what are the negatives for an image?","explanation":"The InfoNCE loss treats the matching caption as the correct class among all captions in the batch.","type":"single","options":["The texts of the other images in the same batch","Random noise images","Nothing; there are no negatives","Images of the same class"],"answer":0},{"id":"vit-clip-4","prompt":"ViTs need more data or stronger pretraining than CNNs mainly because…","explanation":"Weaker inductive biases must be learned from data, but they scale very well when data is abundant.","type":"single","options":["they have no parameters","they lack the built-in locality and translation-equivariance biases of convolutions","they cannot use GPUs","attention is inaccurate"],"answer":1}],"video-3d":[{"id":"video-3d-1","prompt":"In tracking-by-detection, which algorithm assigns new detections to existing tracks?","explanation":"It finds the minimum-cost one-to-one assignment; a Kalman filter predicts where each track should be.","type":"single","options":["k-means","The Hungarian algorithm on an IoU/appearance cost matrix","Gradient descent","BFS"],"answer":1},{"id":"video-3d-2","prompt":"What does a NeRF learn?","explanation":"Pixels are rendered by integrating density and colour along camera rays.","type":"single","options":["A function from 3D position and viewing direction to density and colour","A depth map for one image","A mesh with textures","A 2D segmentation mask"],"answer":0},{"id":"video-3d-3","prompt":"PointNet uses a symmetric max-pool so that its output does not depend on the order of the input points.","explanation":"Point clouds are unordered sets, just like a graph's neighbours.","type":"tf","answer":true}],"__exam":[{"id":"cv-exam-1","prompt":"A detector reaches mAP@0.5 of 0.80 but mAP@[0.5:0.95] of 0.35. What does that suggest?","explanation":"Strict IoU thresholds expose loose boxes; better box regression losses or higher-resolution features help.","type":"single","options":["It finds objects but localizes boxes imprecisely","It misses most objects","It has too many classes","The metric is broken"],"answer":0},{"id":"cv-exam-2","prompt":"Which components does a vision-language model like LLaVA combine? (select all)","explanation":"Image patches become \"visual tokens\" that the LLM reads alongside text.","type":"multi","options":["A pretrained vision encoder","A projector into the LLM's embedding space","A language model decoder","A U-Net"],"answer":[0,1,2]},{"id":"cv-exam-3","prompt":"You must segment tumours that occupy 1% of each scan. Which loss addition helps most with the imbalance?","explanation":"Dice measures overlap directly and is far less dominated by the large background.","type":"single","options":["MSE","Dice loss alongside cross-entropy","Hinge loss","No change"],"answer":1},{"id":"cv-exam-4","prompt":"A 336×336 image with 14×14 patches becomes how many visual tokens?","explanation":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>336</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>14</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>24</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>576</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(336/14)^2=24^2=576</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">336/14</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">576</span></span></span></span>. High-resolution tiling multiplies this, which costs context and money.","type":"num","answer":576,"tol":0}]}